WEBVTT

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.990
I am Commander Fikatsia Latrova 
of the Zhar Batallion.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.070
I'll be your escort during the exercises.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.980
Enjoy your time in hell.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.460
<b>August 8th, 2001</b>

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.260
This is the area where the UN Dispatch 
Force will be doing their tests.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.260
In other words, your battlefield.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.240
The northern area will be assigned 
to the Idar Test Flight.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.440
The southern area is the Chinese 
United Front army's Bao-Feng Flight.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.860
And in the center will be Argos Test Flight.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.650
Somebody's got some confidence in us.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:13.020
Yeah, it gives us plenty 
of room to move around.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.390
But if a gap opens up in the lines,

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.880
we'll be surrounded and wiped out.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.510
There's mountains behind us,

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:23.000
and compared to the forces to our 
north and south we're farther ahead.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.830
You're very lucky.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.270
With all the large-scale invasions going on,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.470
you can do all the live-fire 
exercises you want.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.120
This is my chance!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.120
I'll explain the operation.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.120
Phase one will be a depth 
charge strike by our fleets.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.750
That sensation I had for 
just one instant there...

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:48.440
Phase two is area denial via aerial depth 
charges from the fleets and artillery teams.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.410
In order to truly make it my own, I've got 
no choice but to throw myself into real battle.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:52.150
If I can master that, I 
can become a better Eishi!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:55.600
Phase 3: Wipe out all surviving units with 
our mechanized armor and combat helicopters.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.600
Yes, like them.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:03.990
Phase 4: When the surviving enemy forces 
have gone below a certain number,

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.580
Cryska and Inia aren't here?

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.140
we deliberately draw them in and each 
test flight will perform their exercises.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.220
That's how we're going to 
keep you fighting a safe war.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:20.100
Lastly, as the commander of your escort squad

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.010
I need to say something to each 
of the Eishi in the test flights.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.400
Don't get in our way.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:26.880
That's all.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:33.070
We may alter or end the trials in response 
to changing battlefield conditions.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.920
Everyone keep a close eye on your data links.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.860
Dismissed.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.160
Is she worried about the fact that I 
don't have any combat experience, too?

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:57.150
With this many skilled Eishi on the front 
lines we'll be getting some good data.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:01.000
Test or no, don't forget the 
fact that this is a real fight.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.200
Yes, of course.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:10.180
<b>Falling Tears</b>

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:16.430
Yeah.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:25.010
The place we're going, Milkovsky, is right near 
the Evensk Hive, and totally on the front lines.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:25.720
Yeah.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:28.020
Forget something?

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:31.850
I almost forgot my EM Radiation Cannon.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.800
Come to think of it, they 
never came to the briefing.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.770
I hope nobody else went after them.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.110
I don't get it.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:52.190
Listen, Yuuya, don't worry 
about your TSF's condition.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.630
Just show the BETA what you can do.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.280
What's with those Scarlet Twins?

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.880
Watch your driving!

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.870
You've got guts, man.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.680
I thought you were nervous 
about your first battle,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.370
and instead you're thinking about women!

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.780
What are you talking about?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.860
Right. You never do seem 
aware of what you're saying.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.760
Did you say something?

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.070
The Scarlet Twins, huh?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.960
From how you've been acting lately I thought 
you only had eyes for Princess Yui.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.030
You asshole, it's not like that!

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.550
I'm just a test pilot on her project...

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.550
Just a test pilot?

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:35.520
Stop the car.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.700
Hey, Yuuya!

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.310
Again?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:43.870
Are they okay?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.780
What's going on?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.650
Damn it! Let me go!

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:01.740
If you tell me that you won't threaten 
us, your comrades, I'll let you go.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.350
Shut up. How many times do I have 
to tell you you're not our comrades?

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.000
Don't think you can boss us around!

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.420
What's wrong with her?

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.130
She's totally different than last time.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.370
Is she really that same scared girl?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.920
Let him go! You'll break his arm!

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.490
What's with you?

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.930
Medical treatment on the 
front lines is very quick.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.440
A clean break will heal in 10 days.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.430
Stop it! Come on, stop!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.400
Next time I'll break it.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.010
Never touch a comrade again.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.690
Shut up, bitch!

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:38.760
Stop it!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.310
Hey, he was there last time!

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.670
Get out of here, you stupid kid.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.360
You'd better watch your back!

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:46.990
Yuuya!

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.570
Yuuya...

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:52.290
Are you okay, Inia?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.500
Yes, because Cryska was here.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.300
I see. I'm glad.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.270
What are you doing, Bridges?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:02.470
I thought they were hassling you again.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.920
I don't need your help.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.560
I can handle a situation like that myself.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.280
I see.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.800
But be careful.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.070
They'll be back in bigger numbers.

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:22.580
If what happened before happens again...

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.660
Before? What?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.810
What are you talking about?

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.370
No, what are you talking about?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.050
Are you planning something?

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.550
What's going on?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.740
Does she not remember what happened?

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.600
No, Cryska. Yuuya...

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.030
But there's no sign of that with Inia.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.720
Inia, you don't have to worry about this.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.360
Come to think of it, you're going 
out on the front lines too, right?

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:58.990
Yeah, that's why we're here, of course.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.340
I see.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.980
Then wait for the right moment and fall back.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:06.760
What? You're telling me to run?

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:07.690
Hell no.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:13.870
I don't want your filthy blood 
staining the soil of the motherland.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.120
Let's go, Inia.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.400
Okay.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.890
Bye, Yuuya!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:42.280
Zhar Battalion and all escort flights have 
deployed to the designated coordinates.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.420
Tse 04 Control to Argos Lead.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.040
Permission to launch has been granted.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.300
After Idar and Bao-Feng have 
launched, proceed to runway.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.790
Argos Lead, roger.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.980
Command Post to Argos Leader.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:59.490
Begin launch preparations. Repeat, 
begin launch preparations.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.060
Argos 1, roger.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.890
You're all ready too, right partner?

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.190
What is it, Argos 2?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.930
Uh, well...

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.420
You're looking good, Yuuya.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.820
You'll survive.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.030
What?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.080
You're that worried about me?

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.920
I'm not worried!

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.650
Bad idea, Tarisa.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:28.440
Confessing your love before 
a mission is always bad luck.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:31.160
You can do it when you get back.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.680
You'll have more fun that way.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:34.980
Shut up!

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:42.740
No abnormal vibrations detected.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.510
Nothing on Sono-Buoys.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:47.680
No enemies sighted on any warning systems.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:59.060
Without this much firepower, we can't 
stop the BETA from advancing...

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:07.980
The Scarlet Twins are in Zone 
1... are they going to be okay?

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.980
It's too late for worrying.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.630
Come on! Am I trying to distract myself?

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:20.630
It's pretty quiet over there. 
Is our guest taking a nap?

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.780
I've heard it's his first fight.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.880
He's probably too scared to fight.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.310
Good to see the kids are lively.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:36.250
I can't believe we got stuck babysitting.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.570
Give me a break.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:41.710
I hope they get hit by a 
stray round and get killed.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.830
Well, most people get killed 
in their first fight.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.180
He won't make it past the 
eight minutes of death.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.010
What a spoiled asshole.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:53.200
We're protecting him and he's ignoring us.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:59.960
Oh, sorry. My seat's so 
comfortable, I was taking a nap.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:04.460
This is my first fight and I'm taking 
it easy. You guys keep it up.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:08.190
Don't you talk to us like that...

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:12.690
BETA forces approaching 
4000 meters to the front.

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.510
The fleets are deploying 
their depth charges.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:15.510
They're here.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.650
37 seconds until the support 
fire point is reached.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:21.710
36.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.850
35.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.050
34.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.270
33.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:26.400
32.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.690
31.

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:28.810
30.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.000
29.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.130
28.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.130
Not yet?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.230
27.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:33.410
26.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.030
Are they here yet?

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.590
25.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:35.540
24.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:36.810
Calm down, Argos 1.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.870
23.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:37.960
22.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.550
What happens happens.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.170
21.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:42.200
Countdowns always make me nervous.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.270
20.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.420
19.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.640
18.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.300
Tell them to have her whisper 
it sweetly into my ear, Argos 4.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.820
17.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.030
16.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:45.900
15.

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:47.720
Don't be silly.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.720
Zero Hour Minus 12.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.170
You guys...

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.170
11.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:51.990
10.

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:53.300
9.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.530
8.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.990
Thanks for caring about me, guys.

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.570
7.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.730
6.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.880
5.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:58.980
4.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:00.150
3.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.250
2.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:01.990
1.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:02.910
0.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.070
This is a real battlefield...

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:24.860
What?

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.230
What's going on?

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.300
What's wrong, Argos 3?

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.460
I knew it!

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.050
There's not enough tanks!

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:32.210
What?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.090
There's not enough firepower at the front!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:49.360
At this rate, they'll let too many through!

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.800
Lt. Sandek, what's going on here?

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.840
This is quite different from the briefing.

00:12:55.780 --> 00:13:00.770
It looks like we haven't replenished 
the losses from yesterday.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.040
I was told it would be ready 
in time for the exercises...

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:08.160
Then I'm requesting the operation be 
called off immediately. Contact command!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.350
Wait, Lieutenant.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:13.820
You never have the amount of forces 
you expect on the front lines.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:17.220
This is the perfect chance 
to test your prototypes.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.900
They might be surrounded and wiped out!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.120
Confirm with command immediately!

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.220
Bridges...

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:27.840
This is bad.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.530
There's a lot of them heading for us.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.630
Why isn't the Soviet Army doing something?

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.750
Their mechanized infantry's gonna get eaten!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:35.980
Argos 1 to Zhar 1.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:38.500
The mechanized infantry needs help.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.820
Argos 1 to Zhar 1! Come in!

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.140
If we don't support them.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:47.130
Don't freak out because there 
aren't enough of them, kid.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.510
Zhar 1 to all battalion members.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.850
Support the mechanized infantry's withdraw.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.230
The direct support teams are to keep 
our useless guests out of the way.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.070
Don't let them stray too far.

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:57.900
Useless?

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:02.040
Show them what a real fight is.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.030
Roger!

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:06.190
Attention all UN Test flights.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.230
You can do what you want.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.030
But don't get in our way.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:10.950
Hey!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.440
Company sized BETA force approaching.

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:16.050
Approximately 150.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:18.790
Composed of Destroyers and Grapplers.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.050
They're here.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.040
The bastards.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.070
Stay calm.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:29.250
Our mission is to escort Argos 1.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.600
I know.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:33.300
We won't let any of them get near Yuuya!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:36.870
Spread out in formation 
Circle 1 around Argos 1.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:37.710
Hurry.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:38.700
Roger.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.310
I really am useless like this.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.930
What am I doing here?

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:55.990
Lt. Sandek, request that the operation 
be called off immediately.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.690
This situation is clearly more dangerous 
than our initial safety projections permitted.

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:05.140
We have a squad of ace 
pilots at a nearby base.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.920
There are no Laser class here.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.590
Aerial bombardment is very 
possible here in Kamchatka.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.340
Please remain calm.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.110
Then at least have them on 
standby above the area...

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:20.850
Lieutenant, Soviet Far East 
Command will make that decision.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:26.620
We in the UN dispatch teams 
should focus on our mission.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.530
He's right.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:35.470
But something's wrong here.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:38.250
I hope it's just my imagination.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:48.640
There's no need to waste valuable air 
fuel and explosives just to help the UN.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:54.550
If a bomber is lost in a crash, then the party 
will want someone to take responsibility for it...

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:58.280
If that's really what the Kremlin 
thinks, then I will obey it.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:15:59.640
Comrade Rogofsky.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:03.130
But with resupply as hard 
to come by as it is,

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:06.890
losing mechanized infantry and 
TSFs is also a serious issue.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.460
Don't worry about that.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.840
Our test squads have excellent Eishi.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.710
Consciousness coordinates on target.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.300
Prafka level stabilized at 4.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:37.720
Get out of here!

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.020
Jacob!

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:47.940
Stay calm!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:51.070
Jacob's will remains with us!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.610
Show these lesser life 
forms the might of Zhar!

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:55.870
Nash Ura! {Russian for "For the motherland!"}

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:10.390
Keep up with them, Bao-Feng Flight!

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.500
I can at least provide some support fire.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:27.210
No, I'll hit my allies...

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:29.450
Stay there, damn it!

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:33.650
If it weren't for you, we could've 
put more people in the front!

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:37.970
Because of you, Jacob... Jacob!

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:43.920
That's...

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.740
Argos 1 to Command Post!

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:50.200
Large number of enemy reinforcements on the 
retreating mechanized infantry's right flank.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.270
They'll be surrounded and wiped out!

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.670
Have Zhar Battalion fall back!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:58.420
If I get a clear line of fire I can support 
them with the EM Radiation Cannon!

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:00.820
Command Post Roger.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.960
Argos 1, maintain present coordinates.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.400
Wait for firing permission.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.540
Hurry! There's no time!

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.140
What are you doing, Commander?

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:16.940
Why aren't you moving?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.610
I don't have a choice...

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.990
Argos 1 to Zhar 1!

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.710
Come in, please!

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.270
Commander Latrova!

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.720
What do you want?

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:29.180
I told you not to bother us!

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.800
Enemy reinforcements!

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:32.520
The mechanized infantry 
is going to get wiped out.

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.850
Fall back and wait for air support...

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.370
There's been no retreat order. That is all.

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:40.380
You know what's going to happen 
if you wait for orders!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.920
Please.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.900
We can still make it.

00:18:55.470 --> 00:19:00.160
Even now there's no fire support 
and no withdrawal order.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.380
Those pigs in command are 
planning to sacrifice us

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:08.670
just to stop the test 
firing of the new cannon.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.280
I won't let them.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:13.830
Zhar 1 to all units.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.800
We're going to split up.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.390
Each company is to withdraw 
to the coordinates I send.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:21.310
Commander, the mechanized infantry 
hasn't finished withdrawing.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.280
I know. But don't worry.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.820
The boy says he's going to save us all.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.680
Commander!

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:30.900
There's no time!

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:31.940
Hurry up and withdraw!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:32.800
Roger!

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.000
Is it no good?

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:42.550
Will they not listen to me after all?

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.230
Command Post to Argos 1!

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.770
Zhar Battalion has received 
the withdrawal order.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.080
You are cleared to fire!

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.590
Argos 1, roger!

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.930
Please, make it!

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.070
Activating the superconducting motor!

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:11.180
Artillery fire's always been an 
American favorite, hasn't it?

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:12.940
Cartridge Load.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.190
We're counting on you, Yuuya.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.190
Fixing Mount Arm.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.620
Blow 'em away, Yuuya!

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:39.090
Let's go, monsters!

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.600
What was that?

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.910
What happened, Commander?

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.910
You did it!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.270
That kid...

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.630
Yeah! We did it!

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:44.240
Command Post to Argos 1.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:45.980
Lt. Takamura?

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:47.080
Why are you...

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.060
Um, well...

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.890
Argos 1, report your situation.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.030
Roger.

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:55.020
All units are fine.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:55.820
No damage.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:59.180
Not to your precious railgun either.

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:02.820
I see.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:06.000
Anyway, well done Argos 1.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.570
Good job for your first time out.

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:10.970
T-That's my line lieutenant.

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:15.510
The railgun you worked on saved everyone.

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:17.770
Not bad work.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:20.540
By the Japanese, or you.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.960
Now give me your next order.

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:28.840
M-Mission complete.

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:31.550
Argos Test Flight is to return to base.

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:34.020
Argos 1, roger.

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:10.400
My mission is to make the 94 
Second the best it can be.

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:13.560
The 94 Second will engage as a chaser.

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:15.930
But I will pilot it this time.

00:24:15.930 --> 00:24:21.440
So Lt. Takamura insists on not 
letting Ensign Bridges fight?

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:24.310
<b>Premonition</b>

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:23.680
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:24.310
Premonition
